# SEO

Read **Project Profile → SEO** in `CURSOR.md` and `settings.json` → `seo.enabled`.

## When SEO = `off`

- Do not add title/meta/OG/Twitter/JSON-LD pipelines
- Do not prioritize sitemap/robots work unless the user turns SEO on
- Marketing pages may still have a sensible document title for UX only

## When SEO = `on`

- Unique `<title>` and meta description per public route
- Canonical URL where duplicates exist
- Open Graph + Twitter cards for shareable pages
- `robots.txt` / sitemap when the project has multiple public URLs
- **Schema.org** JSON-LD on relevant pages (required)

### Schema.org (required if SEO on)

| Page kind | Example `@type` |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Site-wide | `Organization`, `WebSite` |
| Article / blog | `Article` / `BlogPosting` |
| Product / service | `Product` / `Service` |
| FAQ | `FAQPage` |
| Local business | `LocalBusiness` |

- Emit valid JSON-LD (`application/ld+json`)
- Keep IDs/URLs consistent with canonical
- Do not invent fake ratings or reviews

To disable later: set SEO to `off` in Project Profile + `settings.json` and stop extending SEO machinery.
